WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.972 --> 00:00:03.600
(transition whooshing)

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.940
- In this project, we
put capacitive sensing

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:07.830
on top of robotic skins.

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:10.740
Traditionally, robotic fingers are rigid.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.080
In this project, we are using silicone

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.750
with flexible electrodes
made out of copper,

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:18.480
which are connected to a
capacitive sensing chip

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:19.620
that is normally made

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:22.020
for smartphone capacitive touch sensors.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:25.410
This approach makes it
affordable and scalable.

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:29.700
- We use computational design
to fabricate our electrodes.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:34.650
And this particular
design has the capability

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:37.890
to enable computer
vision on the electrodes

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:40.650
because we have a fairly high definition

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:42.600
and we can do blob tracking

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:47.553
or detection of a slippery
problem in a robotic touch.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:51.780
- To laser cut our design, we
export the file and load them

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:54.510
onto this laser cut control software.

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:56.400
Here we can see two objects.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.370
One will be vertically
placed on the robotic finger.

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:02.790
It corresponds to the
x-axis of the sensor.

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:04.860
The other will come perpendicularly

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:07.140
to measure the y-axis data.

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:09.600
These will be combined
to show the whole picture

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:11.880
that has enough data for blob detection

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:13.680
and signal processing.

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:15.270
- Now that we are ready,

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:19.200
we can put the Kapton tape on the glass

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.820
and some copper tape,

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:23.850
and we can engrave it using this laser.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.505
I'm going to put it in the machine.

00:01:25.505 --> 00:01:27.990
(gentle music)

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:30.126
And now I can start engraving.

00:01:30.126 --> 00:01:32.935
(gentle music continues)

00:01:32.935 --> 00:01:34.980
Now that we have engraved the copper tape,

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:36.960
we can peel off the electrode

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:41.100
and place it directly
on the silicone finger.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:42.570
Then we can encapsulate it

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:45.300
either with this piece of latex glove

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:48.630
or we can dip it in silicone.

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:51.330
And eventually, the idea is to have

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:55.920
a fully sensitive robotic hand
that can recognize objects

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:59.430
that it's touching, recognize
when the objects are falling,

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:03.930
and adding more intelligence
to the robotic hand.

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:07.230
- Infusing increased intelligence
and autonomous function

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:10.590
in robotic hands to lead
to significant enhancement

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:12.300
in various applications,

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:16.983
such as manufacturing,
healthcare, and space exploration.

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:20.853
We are really excited to
shape this future reality.

